### CampusEvents API – manual requests
### Open in VS Code (extension "REST Client") or PhpStorm and click "Send Request".
@base = http://localhost:8000/backend

### ---------- Authentication (week 07) ----------

### Without a token -> 401
GET {{base}}/events

### Log in as admin – the response contains "token"
# @name login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@campusevents.ba", "password": "Admin123!" }

### Token from the login above (REST Client fills it in automatically)
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### Wrong password -> 401 (see logs/error.log)
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@campusevents.ba", "password": "wrong" }

### Register a new student (the "role" is ignored – always student)
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "first_name": "Amar", "last_name": "Hodžić", "email": "amar@campusevents.ba", "faculty": "FENS", "password": "Secret123", "password_confirm": "Secret123", "role": "admin" }

### Who am I?
GET {{base}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Invalid token -> 401
GET {{base}}/events
Authorization: Bearer abc.def.ghi

### Token check by hand (version 1)
GET {{base}}/v1/my-registrations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------- Resources (send the token every time) ----------

### All events
GET {{base}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One event
GET {{base}}/events/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Reviews of an event
GET {{base}}/events/9/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create an event
POST {{base}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Intro to Docker Workshop",
  "club_id": 2,
  "category_id": 2,
  "location": "FENS Lab 1",
  "starts_at": "2026-12-03 17:00",
  "capacity": 25
}

### Register for an event
POST {{base}}/registrations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "user_id": 3, "event_id": 12 }

### Dashboard
GET {{base}}/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Weather forecast (logged in info.log as EXTERNAL API)
GET {{base}}/weather/forecast?city=Mostar
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------- Step-by-step versions ----------

### v1 – not found, but status 200
GET {{base}}/event_by_id?id=999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### v1 – invalid, but status 200
POST {{base}}/add_event
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "" }

### v2 – 404
GET {{base}}/v2/events/999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### v2 – 400
POST {{base}}/v2/events
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "" }

### ---------- Two-factor authentication & SSO (week 07, optional) ----------

### 1. Start 2FA setup (as the logged-in user) -> secret + otpauth:// link (scan as QR code in an authenticator app)
POST {{base}}/auth/2fa/setup
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2. Enable with the 6-digit code from the app
POST {{base}}/auth/2fa/enable
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "123456" }

### 3. Login without code -> { "two_factor_required": true } (no token!)
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@campusevents.ba", "password": "Admin123!" }

### 4. Login with code -> token
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@campusevents.ba", "password": "Admin123!", "code": "123456" }

### Google SSO (needs GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID; without it -> 503)
POST {{base}}/auth/google
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id_token": "paste-the-id-token-from-google-identity-services" }

### ---------- Authorization (week 08) ----------

### Log in as a student
# @name student
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "lana@campusevents.ba", "password": "Student123!" }

###
@student_token = {{student.response.body.token}}

### Student creates an event -> 403
POST {{base}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{student_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Not allowed", "club_id": 1, "category_id": 1, "location": "Hall", "starts_at": "2026-12-03 17:00", "capacity": 10 }

### Role checked by hand (version 1) -> 403
DELETE {{base}}/v1/categories/5
Authorization: Bearer {{student_token}}

### Student sees only her own registrations
GET {{base}}/registrations
Authorization: Bearer {{student_token}}

### Student opens Ema's registration (id 1) -> 403
GET {{base}}/registrations/1
Authorization: Bearer {{student_token}}

### Student registers – user_id 2 in the body is IGNORED, the registration belongs to Lana
POST {{base}}/registrations
Authorization: Bearer {{student_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "user_id": 2, "event_id": 12 }

### Student checks herself in -> 403 (admins only)
PUT {{base}}/registrations/6/attend
Authorization: Bearer {{student_token}}

### Student deletes Ema's review (id 1) -> 403
DELETE {{base}}/reviews/1
Authorization: Bearer {{student_token}}

### Student dashboard (personal numbers)
GET {{base}}/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{student_token}}

### Student lists users -> 403
GET {{base}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{student_token}}

### Admin deletes own account -> 400
DELETE {{base}}/users/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
